# Supabase security

## Keys

- Frontend: `SUPABASE_URL` + publishable/anon key only.
- Backend may use `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` — never commit, log, return via API, or ship to frontend.
- Service-role bypasses RLS → enforce authorization in FastAPI services.

## Migrations

- All schema changes via `supabase/migrations/` (use `npx supabase migration new <name>`).
- Include table, index, FK, constraint, trigger, function, RLS when needed.
- Must reset cleanly: `npx supabase db reset`.
- No manual production Dashboard schema edits.

## RLS

- Enable RLS on every `public` table the frontend can touch.
- Prefer `auth.uid() = user_id` (or equivalent) for user-owned rows.
- Never disable RLS “just to make it work”.
- Do not authorize from editable `user_metadata`; use DB columns / `app_metadata` / backend checks.
